# Elixir maps and structs

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:obsidian_livebook, github: "scossar/obsidian_livebook"},
  :kino
])
```

## Structs are an extension built on top of maps

Docs:

* [Keyword lists and maps](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/keywords-and-maps.html)
* [Structs](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/structs.html)

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

### Maps

Maps are the go to data structure for key-value pairs:

```elixir
map = %{:a => 1, 2 => :b}
```

```elixir
map |> inspect |> IO.puts
map[:a] |> IO.puts
map[2] |> IO.puts
```

#### Pattern matching with maps

A map matches as long as the keys in the pattern exist in the given map.

```elixir
%{:a => a} = map
a |> IO.puts
```

#### Map functions

Docs: [Map.html#functions](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/Map.html#functions)

```elixir
map = %{:a => 1, :b => 2, :c => 3} |> Kino.inspect(label: "Base map")
```

## delete(map, key)

```elixir
del_example = Map.delete(map, :a) |> Kino.inspect(label: "Map with the :a entry removed")
```

## fetch(map, key)

```elixir
case Map.fetch(map, :a) do 
  {:ok, val} -> Kino.inspect(val, label: "The value of :a is")
  :error -> Kino.inspect(:error)
end

case Map.fetch(map, :z) do 
  {:ok, val} -> Kino.inspect(val, label: "The value of :z is")
  :error -> Kino.inspect(:error)
end
```

## filter(map, fun)

```elixir
Map.filter(map, fn {_key, val} -> val != 2 end) |> Kino.inspect
```

